        "routed_through_the_effect": true,
        "where_the_windows_came_from": "Measured in this run's own first two takes rather than taken from the printed delay time: the balance was put at each end, the rises in the take were found, and the windows placed from them. A type whose return begins before the note has ended is refused here rather than read.",
        "loaded_once_per_setting": "The block was written and read back once per setting, not once per take, so the repeats say how well a take repeats rather than how well a write does.",
        "read_one_count_at_a_time": "Every count from 56 to 72 and from 108 to 120, and the two ends. Eight counts between settings, which is what the sweep before this one read, cannot tell a level that changes at one setting from one that changes over several; one count can. The ends are in it because they are the reading's own scale: every other setting is read as a share of the one at the dry end."
